        "I didn't ask him about the note. I couldn't, not without revealing I had it, not without risking whoever had sent it, someone clearly taking a real risk to reach me at all, given how carefully they'd chosen their words, how deliberately they'd avoided any detail that might identify them. I folded it small and kept it in the lining of my bag, a second secret now sitting alongside the ones I already carried, and went back to performing the brittle peace of those weeks with a new, colder vigilance underneath it, watching, waiting, patient in a way that surprised even me — the same patience, I understand now, that would eventually become the entire architecture of who I became."
